WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:01.960
- Very nice to meet you.
- Such a pleasure, my guy.

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:02.793
- [Gary] How are you?

00:00:02.793 --> 00:00:04.295
- [Rob] Great, man.

00:00:04.295 --> 00:00:06.962
(hip hop music)

00:00:08.236 --> 00:00:09.069
It's confirmation.

00:00:09.069 --> 00:00:12.790
It's like the stuff that
you already maybe knew

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:13.623
in your gut--

00:00:13.623 --> 00:00:14.456
- 100%

00:00:14.456 --> 00:00:15.289
- What you were pushing toward,

00:00:15.289 --> 00:00:17.560
it's like, okay, I'm not the
only one who feels like this.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:18.503
I'm not crazy.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:23.430
I saw you write about some
people I know, Deon Graham,

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:26.433
is someone who I've known
and worked with a bit.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.156
It was dope.

00:00:30.156 --> 00:00:32.720
It's great to have it as
a resource, as a reminder

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.553
that you're not the only one in the world

00:00:33.553 --> 00:00:35.160
who feels like this.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.400
- I totally agree.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.850
I think affirmation is like ...

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.793
You know?
- Yeah.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.410
To me, I always just think if
you get one nuance it's gold,

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.650
you know?
- Right.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.230
So what's going on?

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:48.820
- Nothing, man, just working, man.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.223
I'm trying to balance it,

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:55.897
the passion and the business
and not lose yourself in it

00:00:55.897 --> 00:00:57.113
and love every minute.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.170
- How's it going?

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:00.027
- Great.

00:01:00.027 --> 00:01:00.860
- Good.
So far, so good.

00:01:01.699 --> 00:01:03.570
- When did it start, a couple months ago?

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:07.023
- I started about last year,
I started with the music.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.090
I've been doing journalism--

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.670
- Well, I know, the
Genius work and all that?

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.130
- Yeah, but I started the music last year.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.340
We were actually supposed to meet ...

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.680
I don't know if you remember
this, we were supposed to meet

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.470
last year and Mike was
trying to set it up,

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:20.303
and I had to cancel--

00:01:20.303 --> 00:01:22.370
- Because you were making the transition.

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:24.790
- Yeah, well what happened
was Logic called me.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:27.277
He had sold out at the Barclay's and said,

00:01:27.277 --> 00:01:28.740
"Yo, do you wanna come on stage with me?"

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.243
- And you were like, yeah!

00:01:31.214 --> 00:01:32.047
(laughing)

00:01:32.047 --> 00:01:33.820
- I didn't wanna cancel but I said ...

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.183
- Nah man, that was the right cancel.

00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:36.340
I would fucking cancel that.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:37.240
- Yeah, man.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.073
- That's amazing.

00:01:38.073 --> 00:01:39.143
- I was in the crowd, I saw it.

00:01:39.143 --> 00:01:40.300
I saw him bring you out.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.133
- Yeah.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:41.966
- You made the right choice.

00:01:41.966 --> 00:01:42.799
I mean, that was a packed house--

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:44.840
- What do you mean he
made the right choice?

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:45.796
You're my guy.

00:01:45.796 --> 00:01:46.629
- He doesn't even wanna
perform his song, man.

00:01:46.629 --> 00:01:47.960
- 100%, that's huge.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:48.990
- Such a moment--
- Yeah.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.020
- How'd it feel?

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.067
- It felt great because I'm
from Flatbush Brooklyn--

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:52.900
- Now I'm aware.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:53.990
- My place is right
there on Flatbush Avenue.

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:55.613
- That's crazy, you
must've been just like,

00:01:55.613 --> 00:01:56.446
what the fuck, huh?

00:01:56.446 --> 00:01:58.270
- It wasn't even there when I was a kid.

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:00.200
Imagine if when you're
a kid somebody says,

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.570
yo, we're gonna take Madison Square Garden

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:03.890
and put it right on Flatbush Avenue

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.050
and all your favorite
artists will perform there--

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.140
- And you'll perform there.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:09.100
That's just crazy.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.920
- I used to battle on that corner

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.600
of Flatbush and Atlantic
Avenue because I went to school

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:13.890
at Brooklyn Tech.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.068
On the way home from school--

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.720
- Who's the person that
roasted you the most

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.410
in the history of your
life on that corner?

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.480
- We know him.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.290
It wasn't on that corner.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.940
Nobody roasted me on that corner.

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:26.060
I was good.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.700
I definitely used to battle
and there's an emcee,

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.380
people know him, I don't
know if you heard of him.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.700
His name is The Immortal Technique.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.750
- Yes, destroyed you?

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:34.683
- He destroyed me.

00:02:35.678 --> 00:02:38.110
- He had his day and you
didn't have your day?

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:39.530
It's like a boxing match.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.760
- No, at the time, he
was just better than me.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:42.593
- Period.

00:02:42.593 --> 00:02:43.426
- It's just period what it was.

00:02:43.426 --> 00:02:44.259
- Yeah, you got it.

00:02:44.259 --> 00:02:45.960
You just went up in weight class.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:46.793
- Yeah.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.520
- How'd you feel?

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.353
- When I lost?

00:02:50.353 --> 00:02:51.342
- Yeah.

00:02:51.342 --> 00:02:52.175
- I mean,

00:02:52.175 --> 00:02:55.560
it stung but I knew he was better than me.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.280
- Yeah, you were looking for the upset.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.510
- Yeah, I wasn't salty.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.573
Well, what happened was
I didn't have a choice.

00:03:00.573 --> 00:03:02.110
When you're challenging and you're there

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:03.100
and people were watching.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.280
We were in a club called The
Wetlands, it doesn't exist

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.390
anymore, but we're in
the basement of this club

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:10.240
and everybody's watching.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.440
Well, you gotta go for it.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.820
- 100%, because the
alternative's way worse.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:14.710
- Yeah.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.490
- Getting knocked out
is a helluva lot worse

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:17.590
than leaving the ring.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.800
A lot better, excuse me.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.320
- The one lesson that I
did learn because he and I

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:25.140
were friends before that and so I laughed.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.100
It was fun to me.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.520
- You took it too light.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.930
- He took it seriously.

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:29.763
- I get it.

00:03:29.763 --> 00:03:31.690
I'm the same--
- I saw the look in his eyes.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.587
- He would kill me in that moment.

00:03:33.587 --> 00:03:36.020
- That's so funny, all
my friends growing up

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:39.900
always would say that about
me when we would play things.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:40.733
- Right.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.720
- I literally thought a
backyard basketball game

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:50.950
was fucking Roman Empire,
like if I lose this game

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:52.406
one-on-one, I'd die.

00:03:52.406 --> 00:03:54.060
- Right.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:55.810
- That's how I do everything still.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:57.533
I get that.

00:03:57.533 --> 00:03:58.990
That makes a lot of sense to me, man.

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:03.990
- But what I found is in my
career of journalism, I approach

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.820
it very much the same way.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:07.580
When I'm creating content,
when I'm doing something

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.503
with an artist, I want the best interview,

00:04:09.503 --> 00:04:10.595
I want the best content--

00:04:10.595 --> 00:04:12.250
- That's exactly right.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:14.480
If blah, blah, blah had the
best interview ever, you're like

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.550
fuck that.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:17.470
I'm gonna get something out of this guy

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:19.190
that he's never said before.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.470
- And guess what?

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:21.890
This is real and I believe it.

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:23.990
I had the best Kendrick
Lamar interview ever.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:25.280
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.533
I had the best 21 Savage interview ever.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.550
This is how I feel and I dare anybody

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:32.446
to say something different or do better--

00:04:32.446 --> 00:04:34.165
- The one where you took
him to Sharp with the knives

00:04:34.165 --> 00:04:34.998
and everything.

00:04:34.998 --> 00:04:37.810
- Yeah, we took 21 Savage,
I took him to a blacksmith

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.720
with Genius and our team took him,

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.260
and he has the knife tattoo on his head

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.810
and we recreated the knife tattoo

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:47.990
into an actual knife, got an
actual blacksmith to do it

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:50.710
and through that we had
a conversation about

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:52.950
what the tattoo means to him,

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:55.423
him growing up, why he
raps the way he raps.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:57.940
- Look, you're a storyteller.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:58.773
- Right.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.700
It's funny that you realize
that when I made the transition,

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.640
the thing was I grew up
and I always used to rap.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:07.700
I thought I was gonna be a rapper first.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.590
The problem was I had my first son.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:11.767
- How old?

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:12.630
- My son is 12 now.
Were you?

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:13.463
You.

00:05:13.463 --> 00:05:14.700
- Oh, me, I'm 38.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:15.533
- Right.

00:05:15.533 --> 00:05:17.380
- And rap wasn't paying the bills

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.624
and journalism came knocking

00:05:18.624 --> 00:05:20.760
and I was like, I'm not
turning this check down,

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:23.220
I got bills to pay, I got mouths to feed.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.390
When I got into the industry,
I still would do music

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:29.870
but I was made to feel like
I was doing something wrong.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:32.250
You couldn't be a journalist
and do music at the same time--

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:33.083
- You're preaching.

00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:34.820
- I literally was almost fired--

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.120
- While you're distracted.

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:38.090
- Because they didn't understand it.

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:40.290
And when it came time to choose the music

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:42.357
which was the passion or the
money and paying the bills ...

00:05:42.357 --> 00:05:43.310
- You took the money.

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:44.423
- I had to.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.920
- My man, everybody does.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.370
Why do you think the people that don't

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:51.500
get put on a pedestal?

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:56.067
- Yeah and I was just afraid
and I wasn't afraid for me--

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:57.100
Of course.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.280
My guy, of course.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:00.113
Of course.

00:06:00.113 --> 00:06:02.710
- But what happens is now ...

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.410
- And there's a million
versions of that story.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:05.243
- Absolutely.

00:06:05.243 --> 00:06:08.400
- There's a person that
decides to go rob somebody

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.010
and goes to jail for three years.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.900
There's a million versions of that story.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:18.900
The reason the person that
doesn't choose those paths,

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:23.030
goes and is one of the few
people that gets through,

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:27.580
is put on a pedestal, it's
because 99% don't even try

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:30.678
and 99% of the 1% don't make it.

00:06:30.678 --> 00:06:33.300
- Right.
- Right.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.750
But what happened to me was

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:37.983
I was good at journalism.

00:06:39.444 --> 00:06:40.810
- Because it was the same fucking game.

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:42.230
- Right, and this is what I realized

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:44.066
because it's storytelling
and going back to the point

00:06:44.066 --> 00:06:45.520
that you said, it's all storytelling.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:47.110
Now, I get to a point
in my journalism career

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:50.720
where I'm at Genius and the
day that I joined Genius,

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:55.340
every rapper worth talking
about was tweeting about me

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:56.930
moving to Genius.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:00.410
Meek Mill had tweeted about
it and this was three days

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:01.290
after Back to Back.

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:03.470
He wasn't on Twitter for those
three days but he tweeted

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:06.470
to say, yo, congratulations,
Rob, congratulations, Genius.

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:07.536
This is dope.

00:07:07.536 --> 00:07:09.170
- That's so great, man,
that's so fucking awesome.

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:11.290
- What I realized at that point was

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:16.223
it's time to follow the passion.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.950
- Even right then and there?

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:19.783
- Maybe not at that moment--

00:07:19.783 --> 00:07:21.610
- But that became the seed.

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:23.120
- First of all, I'm at
a point in journalism

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:25.570
where nobody's gonna
fire me for making music.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.210
Really what it came down to was

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:29.680
I had accomplished everything in my life.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:31.070
I accomplished more
than I thought I could--

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:32.440
- In that field.

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:34.670
- Yeah, but in life at this point.

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:35.503
- Yeah, I get it.

00:07:35.503 --> 00:07:37.330
- More than I thought I
could, more than I think a lot

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:39.660
of people gave me credit
for when I was growing up.

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:43.650
But I didn't wanna look
back at my life and not do

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.730
the one thing that I always wanted to do

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:47.490
which was make music.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:50.320
- Honestly, I think the biggest confusion

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.630
of the way people consume my content is

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:56.200
I believe in the way that
you did it more than the way

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:59.440
that people interpret what
I'm telling them to do is.

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:02.110
People hear the part of my
content that says go jump,

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:03.280
quit your job.

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:04.689
They don't hear the practical part.

00:08:04.689 --> 00:08:06.663
- Right.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.430
- They didn't hear the other
part of the sentence which was

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:13.960
if you're willing to live
in a shittier situation

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:16.130
in the short term ...

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:17.790
You could've made the jump,

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:20.200
but you and your girl and your baby

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.680
would've had it even shittier.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:22.740
You coulda.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:24.450
You didn't have to take a check from XXL.

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:25.283
You coulda kept going.

00:08:25.283 --> 00:08:26.510
- And the check wasn't that big.

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:28.092
- That's right, you coulda
worked at the fucking--

00:08:28.092 --> 00:08:29.800
- We rectified that, baby.

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:31.800
- But you coulda worked at the bodega.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:32.950
You coulda.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:35.960
You coulda fucking played Cee-Lo
in the corner, try to win.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:37.160
You coulda.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:40.060
You could have moved in with your moms.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:41.046
You could have.

00:08:41.046 --> 00:08:42.310
- Right.

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:43.903
- They hear the jump.

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:49.850
They don't hear the but
everything else besides the jump

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.420
is about to get worse.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:56.680
The 22 year olds hear me say,
yo, this is the practical time

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:57.830
to jump.

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:59.820
All these kids that are shitting
on their parents because

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:02.700
of my content don't hear
the part that I agree

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.890
with their parents on
which is wait, oh, kid

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:08.290
who I just paid college
for, you're telling me

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:10.070
some fucking asshole
Gary V on the Internet

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:12.440
said don't get a job and now
you're gonna be a rapper?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.029
Cool, but I'm not giving
you any more money.

00:09:15.029 --> 00:09:16.760
- Right.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:19.890
- These kids hear it and they
want moms and dads to still

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:23.413
give them $1,000 Starbucks
card or pay for the gym.

00:09:25.038 --> 00:09:26.376
- Nah, you gotta thug it out.

00:09:26.376 --> 00:09:30.900
- So people are hearing the
part they wanna hear from me.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.410
That's why so many people
don't fuck with me at first

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:35.390
because I'm putting pressure
on them and they'd go rather

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:37.630
listen to some other bullshit person--

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:38.830
- They wanna be coddled.

00:09:40.062 --> 00:09:43.310
